<!-- PRINCIPLES + CODE EDITOR -->
<section class="principles-section">
  <div class="ps-inner">
    <div class="ps-left">
      <div class="ps-label reveal">Engineering Principles</div>
      <div class="principle reveal">
        <div class="p-n">01</div>
        <div><div class="p-title">Verification over trust</div><div class="p-desc">Every data payload, agent action, and system state must be independently verifiable. No trust assumptions — cryptographic proof or it didn't happen. This is why we build on Bittensor and blockmachine's verified RPC layer.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="principle reveal reveal-d1">
        <div class="p-n">02</div>
        <div><div class="p-title">Incentive alignment</div><div class="p-desc">Agent behavior follows economic incentives. Systems are designed so correct behavior is the profitable behavior — aligned with Bittensor's miner/validator model and blockmachine's SN19 scoring protocol.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="principle reveal reveal-d2">
        <div class="p-n">03</div>
        <div><div class="p-title">Physical-digital continuity</div><div class="p-desc">City infrastructure, IIoT systems, and blockchain compute are one continuous layer — not separate domains. Operon's city-infrastructure module embodies this: turbine SCADA → digital twin → Bittensor-verified routing → actuation.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="principle reveal reveal-d3">
        <div class="p-n">04</div>
        <div><div class="p-title">Open by default</div><div class="p-desc">All Coreweaver Labs work is open-source under MIT unless a security constraint demands otherwise. TypeScript + Zod for type-safe, self-documenting systems. DRY. Composable. No proprietary lock-in.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
